# Security Rules — CRITICAL

## Never Violate
- Never hardcode secrets — use `.env` / `config()`
- Never commit `.env` to version control
- Never log passwords, tokens, or PII
- Always validate via FormRequest before processing
- Always use `$fillable` on models (mass assignment protection)

## Key Patterns
```php
// Use Policies for authorization
$this->authorize('delete', $post);

// Rate limit auth endpoints
Route::middleware(['throttle:5,1'])->group(function () {
    Route::post('/login', [AuthController::class, 'login']);
});

// Protect routes with Sanctum
Route::middleware('auth:sanctum')->group(function () {
    Route::apiResource('orders', OrderController::class);
});

// Hash passwords (use 'hashed' cast, don't manual hash)
protected $casts = ['password' => 'hashed'];
```

## Dependency Audit
```bash
composer audit    # Check PHP packages
npm audit         # Check JS packages
```
